{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>In righteousness shall you judge your fellow.</b> He warns that justice must be in righteousness, that is, that he should justify a person's judgment and not distort it. For whoever judges in righteousness upholds the throne of the King, as it says (Psalms 89:15): ״צדק ומשפט מכון כסאך״. And if he distorts the judgment, he blemishes the throne of the King and treats His honor lightly. And they said in the Midrash: if he judges in righteousness, the Shekhinah is with him, as it says (Psalms 82:1): ״אלהים נצב בעדת אל״; and if not, the Shekhinah withdraws, as it says (Psalms 12:6): ״משוד עניים מאנקת אביונים עתה אקום יאמר ה׳״. And the spirit of the Holy Spirit cries out and says (Psalms 57:12): ״רומה על שמים אלהים על כל הארץ כבודך״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The citations in the final paragraph appear without verse numbers in the source; identified as Psalms 82:1, Psalms 12:6 (the text reads ה׳ for the final word of the verse), and Psalms 57:12 respectively."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:55.817544768Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}